WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.224
This session follows the school ECG and blood-gas sections of Seven D Part B. Use the earlier rhythm and lead-placement skills, but now connect electrical and chemical findings to one changing patient.
本节依7D Part B的ECG及血气课程。应调用此前心律和导联定位技能，现在把电及化学发现联系到同一位变化患者。

00:00:13.224 --> 00:00:24.216
The goal is not to collect more labels. Explain whether a result is reliable, what process it supports and what clinical threat needs attention while uncertainty remains.
目标不是收集更多标签，而是解释结果是否可靠、支持什么过程，以及不确定仍存在时哪些临床威胁需要处理。

00:00:24.216 --> 00:00:36.960
You will classify four basic acid-base patterns and see why a normal pH or a nondiagnostic ECG does not guarantee safety. The pattern is a tool, not the complete diagnosis.
你会分类四种基本酸碱模式，并看到为何pH正常或ECG无诊断性都不保证安全。模式是工具，不是完整诊断。

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:50.400
Interpretation teaching does not grant invasive sampling, analyzer use, advanced medication or an automatic destination bypass. Keep the actual role and pathway visible throughout.
判读教学不授予侵入取样、分析仪、高级药物或自动绕行权限。整个过程都应明确实际角色及路径。

00:00:50.400 --> 00:01:02.760
Confirm patient identity, acquisition time and the symptom or treatment state. A trace from before a major clinical change may remain useful but does not describe the whole current encounter.
确认患者身份、采集时间及症状或治疗状态。重大临床变化之前的记录仍可有用，但不能描述现在的全部现场。

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:14.856
Check electrode placement, missing leads, movement artifact and baseline wander. Poor placement can create a convincing pattern that more confident interpretation will not repair.
检查电极位置、缺失导联、运动伪差及基线漂移。错误定位可制造很像真的模式，再自信解释也修不好。

00:01:14.856 --> 00:01:25.224
Use the actual recording speed and gain when measuring intervals and elevation. The standard teaching grid is only valid when the printed calibration agrees with it.
测间期或抬高时，应使用真实记录速度及增益。只有打印校准一致，标准教学方格才适用。

00:01:25.224 --> 00:01:37.152
Obtain the useful recording promptly without abandoning airway, breathing or perfusion care. A fast unreadable printout is not a completed diagnostic ECG.
应迅速取得有用记录，但不能放弃气道、呼吸或灌注照护。快速打印一张读不出的纸，不算完成诊断ECG。

00:01:37.152 --> 00:01:50.616
Start with rate and regularity, then identify atrial activity and its relationship to ventricular activation. Do not diagnose an AV block from one dropped-looking complex without checking the pattern.
先看频率及规则度，再识别心房活动与心室激动关系。不能只见一个像脱落的波群就诊断房室阻滞，需检查整个模式。

00:01:50.616 --> 00:02:04.272
Measure PR from the start of P to the start of QRS and assess QRS width using the calibration. A label generated by the device is a prompt to review, not an independent final interpretation.
PR从P起点测到QRS起点，并依校准看QRS宽度。设备生成的名称只是复核提示，不是独立终审。

00:02:04.272 --> 00:02:16.368
Review ST and T changes by anatomically related leads, not one isolated spike. The J point marks the end of QRS and the beginning of the ST segment.
ST及T改变要按解剖相关导联看，不能只盯一个尖峰。J点是QRS结束和ST开始处。

00:02:16.368 --> 00:02:27.720
Then state whether the patient is stable or deteriorating and whether the rhythm is causing, contributing to or compensating for the problem. Rate alone does not settle that distinction.
随后说明患者稳定还是恶化，以及心律在造成、参与还是代偿问题。单凭频率不能区分。

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:41.160
The school uses ischemia, injury and infarction to connect oxygen deprivation with possible ECG changes. Learn the biological ideas without assuming every patient displays a predictable sequence.
学校用缺血、损伤及梗死，把氧不足与可能ECG变化联系起来。应理解生物学概念，但不能假定每位患者都有可预测顺序。

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:54.696
Hyperacute or inverted T waves and ST depression can be concerning in context. These findings are not exclusive to one disease, and a dangerous coronary event can initially have a nondiagnostic tracing.
超急性T、T倒置及ST压低，结合背景可令人担忧，但并非某病独有；危险冠脉事件最初也可能没有诊断性记录。

00:02:54.696 --> 00:03:07.656
ST elevation can reflect acute ischemic injury but has mimics; pathological Q waves may reflect infarction but do not always appear, remain permanent or prove the event time by themselves.
ST抬高可反映急性缺血性损伤，也有模拟情况；病理Q可反映梗死，但未必出现、永久保留，或单独证明发生时间。

00:03:07.656 --> 00:03:19.848
Do not wait for the next supposed cascade stage before escalating concern. The useful decision comes from the whole tracing, symptoms, physiology and the authorized acute-coronary pathway.
不能为等所谓下一演变阶段而推迟升级。有效决定来自整份记录、症状、生理及获授权急性冠脉路径。

00:03:19.848 --> 00:03:33.096
The school emphasizes new J-point ST elevation in at least two contiguous leads. Apply the lead-specific thresholds learned earlier rather than a single one-millimeter rule for every lead and patient.
学校强调至少两个相邻导联的新J点ST抬高。应使用此前导联特定标准，不能对所有导联和患者都套一毫米规则。

00:03:33.096 --> 00:03:44.256
Contiguous means anatomically related views, not simply adjacent boxes on the printed page. Inferior Two, Three and a V F form one familiar group.
相邻是解剖相关视角，不是打印纸上挨着的两个格子。II、III和aVF是熟悉的下壁组。

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:57.576
Reciprocal depression can strengthen concern but is not required in every true event. Also check symptoms, old traces when available and important mimics or conduction abnormalities.
镜像压低可加强怀疑，但不要求每个真实事件都有。也需核对症状、可取得的旧记录，以及重要模拟或传导异常。

00:03:57.576 --> 00:04:10.632
Use the actual STEMI notification and destination criteria promptly. Do not wait for a field troponin or promise that every suspected pattern automatically bypasses every local hospital.
应及时依真实STEMI通知及目的地条件行动，不能等现场肌钙蛋白，也不能保证所有疑似模式都自动绕过每家本地医院。

00:04:10.632 --> 00:04:24.216
Review the standard territory groups so you can state where the abnormality is seen. Regional views overlap and coronary anatomy varies, so one ECG label is not angiographic proof of the culprit artery.
应复习标准区域组，能够说明异常出现在哪里。区域视角会重叠、冠脉解剖也会变化，因此ECG区域名称不是责任动脉的造影证明。

00:04:24.216 --> 00:04:35.544
High lateral changes in One and a V L may meet conventional STEMI criteria. They should not all be called an equivalent simply because the school places them in an advanced review.
I和aVL高侧壁改变可能符合普通STEMI标准，不能只因学校把它们放高级复习，就全部叫等价型。

00:04:35.544 --> 00:04:49.008
Posterior or right-sided concern may require additional trained views and consultation. Keep the standard recording and label additional positions clearly, while urgent care and notification continue.
怀疑后壁或右侧受累时，可能需要额外受训导联及咨询。应保留标准记录，额外位置明确标注，并持续紧急照护和通知。

00:04:49.008 --> 00:05:02.880
The later advanced-twelve-lead workshop develops posterior and conduction-confounded patterns. Here, state the anatomical concern and uncertainty without pretending one absent clue excludes disease.
之后的高级十二导联课会展开后壁及传导干扰模式。这里应说明解剖怀疑与不确定，不能假装缺一条线索就能排除。

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:15.264
A nondiagnostic ECG does not exclude acute coronary syndrome. NSTEMI can have important ST or T abnormalities, and not every troponin elevation is an infarction.
无诊断性ECG不能排除急性冠脉综合征。NSTEMI可有重要ST或T异常，而肌钙蛋白升高也并非全是梗死。

00:05:15.264 --> 00:05:28.512
Unstable angina and infarction require more context than pain intensity or one tracing. A painless or unusual symptom description should not make new hypoperfusion or breathlessness reassuring.
不稳定心绞痛与梗死，需要的背景比疼痛强度或一次记录更多。没有疼痛或症状描述不常见，不能让新低灌注或气促变得放心。

00:05:28.512 --> 00:05:42.696
The current acute-coronary guidance explicitly states that new or presumed new left bundle branch block is not diagnostic of acute infarction in isolation. Clinical correlation and trained interpretation remain necessary.
现行急性冠脉指导明确指出，新发或推定新发左束支阻滞，单独不能诊断急性梗死，仍需临床联系及受训解释。

00:05:42.696 --> 00:05:55.872
Repeat useful ECGs when symptoms persist or change through the actual pathway. Early escalation is appropriate when concern remains high, even while a complete diagnosis is unresolved.
症状持续或变化时，应依真实路径复查有用ECG。诊断未完全明确但仍高度担忧时，也应尽早升级。

00:05:55.872 --> 00:06:07.848
The school lists second-degree type Two block as a dangerous pattern. A dropped QRS alone is insufficient: identify atrial activity and the PR relationship in conducted beats.
学校把二度II型阻滞列为危险模式，但单个QRS脱落还不够，需识别心房活动及已传导搏动中的PR关系。

00:06:07.848 --> 00:06:20.352
A two-to-one pattern may not reveal enough conducted sequences to distinguish the type. Describe the uncertainty and patient state rather than confidently assigning a subtype from missing evidence.
二比一模式可能没有足够已传导序列来区分类型。应描述不确定及患者状态，不能缺证据仍自信定亚型。

00:06:20.352 --> 00:06:33.888
Complete heart block shows atrial and ventricular activity proceeding independently in the appropriate tracing. Escape rate and QRS appearance matter, but the patient perfusion determines the immediate threat.
适当记录中的完全房室阻滞表现为心房与心室独立活动。逸搏率和QRS外观重要，但即时威胁仍取决于患者灌注。

00:06:33.888 --> 00:06:47.208
Recognize deterioration, support primary needs and seek advanced help through the actual protocol. Do not import a generic pacing or atropine instruction into a PCP role without its required authority.
应识别恶化、支持主要需要，并依真实规程寻求高级支援，不能把通用起搏或阿托品指令无权限地导入PCP角色。

00:06:47.208 --> 00:06:58.920
Wide-complex tachycardia can be a dangerous ventricular rhythm, but assess whether a pulse is present and whether perfusion is failing. A rate label cannot replace the patient assessment.
宽波心动过速可属危险室性心律，但要看是否有脉及灌注是否失败。频率标签不能替代患者评估。

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:11.976
Rapid atrial fibrillation is usually irregularly irregular with no consistent sinus P waves, but artifact and other rhythms can mislead. Look at a useful tracing and the whole clinical state.
快速房颤通常绝对不齐且无一致窦性P，但伪差和其他心律可误导。需看有用记录及整体临床状态。

00:07:11.976 --> 00:07:23.088
A bleeding, hypoxic or infected patient may be tachycardic in compensation. Treating the number reflexively can worsen an already inadequate circulation.
失血、低氧或感染患者可能在以快心率代偿。反射性只治数值，会让本已不足的循环更差。

00:07:23.088 --> 00:07:36.792
Pulseless, unstable monomorphic and unstable polymorphic rhythms do not all use the same electrical action. Recognize and communicate accurately while following the trained role-specific pathway.
无脉、不稳定单形及不稳定多形心律，不全用同一种电治疗。应准确识别沟通，并依受训角色特定路径。

00:07:36.792 --> 00:08:28.992
The literal 17.6 opening groups drugs outside the four main Vaughan Williams classes, but they do not share one mechanism. Atropine reduces muscarinic vagal effects and can increase the rate in selected symptomatic bradycardia. Adenosine briefly slows AV-nodal conduction in selected tachycardia pathways; its very short action explains the trained rapid-delivery and flush process, not permission to give it for every fast or wide rhythm. Digoxin can slow AV conduction and has positive inotropic effects; renal impairment, electrolyte disturbances and interactions raise toxicity concerns. The selected manufacturer mechanism and renal sections support that distinction. None is interchangeable with a class-III drug, and this reading adds no independent PCP administration order.
实际17.6开头把不属于四大Vaughan Williams类的药归组，但不表示机制相同。阿托品减少毒蕈碱性迷走作用，可在选定症状性心动过缓中增快心率；腺苷在选定心动过速路径中短暂减慢房室结传导，作用很短解释了受训快速给药和冲管过程，不代表所有快或宽心律都可用。地高辛可减慢房室传导并有正性肌力作用；肾损害、电解质异常和相互作用增加毒性风险，选定厂家机制及肾章节支持这种区别。三者不与III类药互换，本阅读不新增独立PCP给药指令。

00:08:28.992 --> 00:09:12.672
Correct the chapter-summary pressure model before using it in the weekly case. Cardiac output equals heart rate times stroke volume; mean pressure above right-atrial pressure is approximately cardiac output times systemic vascular resistance. The source summary naming only stroke volume and resistance omits heart rate. In an original arithmetic example, 100 beats/minute times 50 mL/beat is 5 L/minute. A lower rate does not guarantee better perfusion if stroke volume cannot compensate. This is a simplified steady-flow explanation, not an exact formula for predicting systolic pressure or deciding a fluid or drug dose.
把总结中的血压模型纠正后再用于本周病例：心排量等于心率乘每搏量；平均压高于右房压的部分，可近似为心排量乘体循环阻力。来源只列每搏量和阻力，漏了心率。原创算例中，100次/分钟乘50 mL/次等于5 L/分钟；如果每搏量无法补偿，心率变低并不保证灌注更好。这是简化稳态血流解释，不是精确预测收缩压或选择补液、药物剂量的公式。

00:09:12.672 --> 00:09:25.872
A single ECG is a sample in time. New pressure, syncope, worsening breathing or reduced perfusion can justify repeating it through the indicated pathway while primary care continues.
一次ECG是时间切片。新压迫感、晕厥、呼吸恶化或灌注下降，可能要求在主要照护持续时依指征复查。

00:09:25.872 --> 00:09:38.280
Compare recordings with attention to placement and quality. A changed electrode position can look like a physiological change and should not be silently treated as definite disease evolution.
比较记录时注意定位和质量。电极改变可能看似生理变化，不能悄悄当成确定病情演变。

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:49.824
Record actual symptom and treatment times so the receiving team can interpret the sequence. Preserve both tracings rather than discarding the earlier one once a new pattern appears.
应记录真实症状和治疗时间，方便接收团队解释顺序。出现新模式后仍应保留两份，不要丢旧记录。

00:09:49.824 --> 00:10:00.528
Communicate the concerning change and current patient state promptly. Uncertainty can be stated clearly without delaying the notification until every label is certain.
应及时通报可疑变化和当前患者状态。不确定可说清，不必等每个名称都确定才通知。

00:10:00.528 --> 00:10:10.032
A blood gas can add evidence about oxygenation, ventilation and acid-base balance. These are related questions but not the same variable.
血气可增加氧合、通气及酸碱平衡证据。三者相关，却不是同一变量。

00:10:10.032 --> 00:10:22.608
PaO2 reflects dissolved arterial oxygen tension, not all tissue oxygen delivery. A normal value does not correct severe anemia, low cardiac output or impaired cellular use.
PaO2反映动脉溶解氧分压，不是全部组织氧输送。数值正常也不能纠正严重贫血、低心排或细胞利用障碍。

00:10:22.608 --> 00:10:34.416
Carbon dioxide helps assess the balance between production and effective ventilation. Its interpretation must include the sample type, perfusion and the recent respiratory treatment.
二氧化碳帮助评估产生与有效通气的平衡，但解释需包含标本类型、灌注及近期呼吸治疗。

00:10:34.416 --> 00:10:47.448
pH and bicarbonate help describe acid-base processes. None of these numbers replaces a primary assessment of whether the patient is becoming more confused, exhausted or hypoperfused.
pH及碳酸氢根帮助描述酸碱过程，但这些数值都不能替代主要评估：患者是否更混乱、疲竭或低灌注。

00:10:47.448 --> 00:10:57.792
An ABG uses an arterial specimen. Confirm the actual source and collection time rather than assuming that a blood-gas printout must be arterial.
ABG使用动脉标本。应确认真实来源和采集时间，不能假设所有血气打印单都是动脉。

00:10:57.792 --> 00:11:11.064
Record oxygen device and settings, ventilation support and important recent changes. A PaO2 obtained on substantial supplemental oxygen means something different from the same number on room air.
应记录给氧装置及设定、通气支持和重要近期变化。大量补氧下的PaO2，与室内空气同一数值意义不同。

00:11:11.064 --> 00:11:22.968
Use the laboratory or analyzer reference and units. A report may display kilopascals instead of millimeters of mercury, and an apparent extreme value can be a unit error.
应依实验室或分析仪参考范围和单位。报告可能用kPa而非mmHg，表面极端数值可能只是单位看错。

00:11:22.968 --> 00:11:34.848
Knowing the interpretation is distinct from being authorized and competent to collect an arterial specimen or operate that analyzer. Do not attempt invasive collection based only on this lesson.
懂解释与获准且有能力采动脉标本或操作分析仪不同，不能只学本节就尝试侵入采样。

00:11:34.848 --> 00:11:46.896
A VBG uses a venous specimen and can support selected acid-base questions. The school correctly warns that arterial and venous results are not interchangeable in every respect.
VBG使用静脉标本，可支持某些酸碱问题。学校也正确提醒，动静脉结果并非处处可以互换。

00:11:46.896 --> 00:12:00.576
Venous carbon dioxide and pH are not guaranteed to equal the arterial values. Sampling site and poor perfusion can widen differences, so do not use a universal add-or-subtract correction.
静脉二氧化碳和pH不保证等于动脉值。取样部位或灌注差可扩大差别，因此不能用通用加减校正。

00:12:00.576 --> 00:12:13.416
Venous PO2 does not describe arterial oxygenation. Do not apply an arterial eighty-to-one-hundred oxygen range to the venous result and declare respiratory failure from that comparison.
静脉PO2不描述动脉氧合。不能把动脉80至100氧范围套到静脉结果，再据此宣布呼吸衰竭。

00:12:13.416 --> 00:12:25.896
State exactly what the sample supports and what remains unknown. Use the patient, reliable oximetry and an appropriate arterial measurement when that is actually required and available.
应准确说明标本支持什么、仍未知什么。需要且可取得时，应结合患者、可靠脉氧及适当动脉测量。

00:12:25.896 --> 00:12:37.248
Check identity, source and time before interpreting a surprising gas. A mislabeled venous specimen cannot be made arterial by applying the expected range.
解释意外血气前先核对身份、来源及时间。标错的静脉标本，不会因套上预期范围就变动脉。

00:12:37.248 --> 00:12:51.024
Air contamination, inadequate sample, anticoagulant problems and delayed analysis can change results. Use the actual collection and analyzer instructions rather than a generic storage rule.
空气污染、量不足、抗凝剂问题及分析延误都可改变结果。应依真实采样及分析仪说明，不套通用储存规则。

00:12:51.024 --> 00:13:03.456
Compare with the clinical state and other reliable observations, and seek an appropriate repeat or laboratory review when needed. Do not repeatedly sample in a way that delays necessary support.
应与临床状态及其他可靠观察比较，需要时适当重采或请实验室复核，但不能反复取样而延误必要支持。

00:13:03.456 --> 00:13:15.528
Record the uncertainty so the next team does not treat a questionable number as a confirmed fact. Validity is part of interpretation, not a separate optional administrative task.
要记录不确定，让下一团队不会把可疑数值当确认事实。有效性是解释的一部分，不是可有可无的行政任务。

00:13:15.528 --> 00:13:27.120
The saved school section uses pH seven point three five to seven point four five, arterial carbon dioxide thirty-five to forty-five, and bicarbonate twenty-two to twenty-six.
保存的学校课程使用pH 7.35至7.45、动脉CO2 35至45，以及碳酸氢根22至26。

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:41.232
Its arterial oxygen example is eighty to one hundred millimeters of mercury. Age, altitude, inspired oxygen and the clinical condition affect the expected oxygen result; this is not a venous reference.
其动脉氧示例为80至100 mmHg。年龄、海拔、吸入氧及临床条件会影响预期氧结果，这不是静脉参考范围。

00:13:41.232 --> 00:13:55.488
The candidate A and P table has different bicarbonate and carbon-dioxide ranges. Keep the school teaching range and the actual laboratory reference labelled instead of blending them into a new invented range.
候选A&P表有不同碳酸氢根及CO2范围。应分别注明学校教学范围及真实实验室参考，不混成新的自创范围。

00:13:55.488 --> 00:14:08.448
A value outside a reference range is not a complete diagnosis; a value inside it does not exclude serious illness. The next step is clinical interpretation and the pattern across the result.
超参考范围不是完整诊断，落在范围内也不能排除严重疾病。下一步应看临床解释及整组模式。

00:14:08.448 --> 00:14:18.792
PaO2 is not a direct tissue-oxygen measurement, despite one school flashcard wording. It describes oxygen tension in the sampled arterial blood.
虽然学校有张闪卡那样写，PaO2并不是直接组织氧测量，而是所取动脉血的氧分压。

00:14:18.792 --> 00:14:32.352
Saturation describes the proportion of hemoglobin binding sites carrying oxygen. Content also depends on how much hemoglobin is present, so severe anemia can reduce carriage despite a good saturation.
饱和度描述血红蛋白结合位点有多少载氧。含量还取决于血红蛋白有多少，因此严重贫血可在饱和度不错时仍减少携氧。

00:14:32.352 --> 00:14:43.248
Delivery also requires effective circulation. A patient in shock may have an acceptable oxygen tension while tissues still receive too little oxygenated blood.
输送还需要有效循环。休克患者氧分压可以尚可，组织却仍收到太少含氧血。

00:14:43.248 --> 00:14:52.704
This distinction matters in the school cardiac-trauma integration. Correcting an oxygen number does not control hemorrhage or restore a failing pump.
这一区别对学校心脏创伤整合很重要。纠正氧数值，不能控制出血或修复失败的泵。

00:14:52.704 --> 00:15:34.584
At the assigned 22.6 boundary, distinguish hyperpnea from hyperventilation. Hyperpnea is increased breathing appropriate to increased metabolic demand; exercise can increase ventilation through anticipatory neural, motor and proprioceptive inputs before a large fall in oxygen occurs. Hyperventilation means effective alveolar ventilation exceeds carbon dioxide production and tends to lower PaCO2. Rate alone cannot distinguish them. The source sentence saying exercise does not cause hyperpnea conflicts with its own discussion; learn the demand-versus-ventilation relationship rather than that absolute sentence.
在指定22.6首页，区分hyperpnea与hyperventilation：前者是适应代谢需求升高的呼吸增加；运动可经预期性神经、运动及本体感受输入，在氧明显下降前就增加通气。后者指有效肺泡通气超过二氧化碳产生，倾向使PaCO2下降，不能单凭频率区分。来源称运动不造成hyperpnea，与其自身讨论矛盾；应学需求与通气的关系，不背该绝对句。

00:15:34.584 --> 00:16:19.824
The same page introduces high altitude: the oxygen fraction of air remains approximately 21 percent while lower barometric pressure lowers inspired oxygen partial pressure. That reduces the available oxygen gradient; it does not mean the atmosphere changed to a smaller oxygen percentage. In the weekly diagnostic case, record altitude, oxygen delivery and exertion with the saturation or blood gas. A textbook example of saturation at one altitude is not an acceptable target for an acutely ill patient. The following altitude table and full acclimatization discussion lie beyond this literal page ending and are not silently added as another completed assigned range.
同页引入高海拔：空气氧比例仍约21%，但气压下降使吸入氧分压下降，减少可用氧梯度，不表示空气中氧百分比变小。本周诊断病例应把海拔、给氧及活动与饱和度或血气一起记录。教材某海拔饱和度例子不是急病患者可接受目标；后续海拔表和完整适应讨论超出实际指定末页，不能暗中改成另一个已完成指定页段。

00:16:19.824 --> 00:17:08.112
Read the ending glossary as connected physiology. ICF is intracellular fluid; IF is interstitial fluid, and ECF includes IF and plasma. Dehydration means insufficient body water, whereas diuresis means increased urine output; neither term alone specifies sodium concentration or emergency fluid needs. ADH, also called vasopressin, supports renal water conservation, and active vitamin D supports intestinal calcium absorption. The source's generic fluid-compartment definition describes the intracellular example too narrowly: plasma and interstitial fluid are also compartments. Match each space, membrane and driving force before predicting where water will move.
把末尾术语连成生理：ICF为细胞内液，IF为组织间液，ECF含IF及血浆。dehydration是体水不足，diuresis是尿量增加，任一词单独都不说明血钠浓度或急救补液需求。ADH又称vasopressin，支持肾保水；活性维生素D支持肠吸钙。来源把一般fluid compartment定义写得只像细胞内例子，过窄，因为血浆和组织间液也属于间隙；预测水移动前先对应空间、膜及驱动力。

00:17:08.112 --> 00:17:54.384
Decode the paired laboratory terms rather than memorizing a symptom as a diagnosis. Hyper- means above and hypo- below the applicable blood reference: natremia for sodium, kalemia for potassium, chloremia for chloride, calcemia for calcium and phosphatemia for phosphate. Hypercapnia and hypocapnia concern carbon dioxide, not oxygen saturation. Respiratory and metabolic acid-base terms identify a process; measured acidemia or alkalemia is a separate statement. In the original breathless patient, low SpO2 does not establish hypercapnia, and confusion does not prove hyponatremia; use the actual measurement and clinical context.
把成对化验词拆开，而不是背症状当诊断：hyper-指高于适用血液参考，hypo-指低于；natremia对应钠，kalemia对应钾，chloremia对应氯，calcemia对应钙，phosphatemia对应磷酸盐。hypercapnia及hypocapnia说二氧化碳，不是氧饱和度；呼吸性和代谢性酸碱词识别过程，而测得酸血症、碱血症是另一项判断。原创气促患者中，低SpO2不证明高碳酸，混乱不证明低钠，须看实际测量和临床背景。

00:17:54.384 --> 00:18:07.896
Carbon dioxide and water are linked through carbonic acid to hydrogen ions and bicarbonate. Carbonic anhydrase speeds the reversible reaction; this connects gas transport and buffering.
二氧化碳和水经碳酸与氢离子、碳酸氢根相联系。碳酸酐酶加速可逆反应，把气体运输和缓冲连起来。

00:18:07.896 --> 00:18:21.528
At otherwise comparable conditions, retaining carbon dioxide tends to increase acidity, while greater effective removal tends to raise pH. Do not copy the candidate figure caption that reverses the latter direction.
其他条件相近时，潴留CO2倾向增加酸度，更有效排出则倾向升高pH。不能照抄把后一方向写反的候选图注。

00:18:21.528 --> 00:18:33.672
Bicarbonate buffers added acid, and the kidneys reclaim and generate bicarbonate while excreting acid. This is not a reason to give bicarbonate automatically whenever the pH is low.
碳酸氢根缓冲加入的酸，肾脏在排酸同时回收并生成碳酸氢根。这不意味着pH低时都自动给碳酸氢钠。

00:18:33.672 --> 00:18:44.784
Chemical buffers respond rapidly, breathing adjustments over minutes and renal changes over longer periods. Time and organ function determine the observed pattern.
化学缓冲很快反应，呼吸调整可在数分钟内发生，肾脏变化更久。时间及器官功能决定所见模式。

00:18:44.784 --> 00:18:58.152
Minute ventilation is rate times tidal volume, but not all that volume reaches gas-exchanging alveoli. Dead-space ventilation explains why rapid shallow breathing can still clear carbon dioxide poorly.
分钟通气量是频率乘潮气量，但不是全部气量都到交换肺泡。死腔通气解释了为何快而浅仍可能排CO2很差。

00:18:58.152 --> 00:19:10.344
In obstruction, slow exhalation and air trapping can limit effective ventilation. A patient can have a high respiratory rate and still develop serious carbon dioxide retention.
阻塞时，呼出慢和气体潴留会限制有效通气。患者即使呼吸频率高，也仍可能严重CO2潴留。

00:19:10.344 --> 00:19:22.824
Watch effort, tidal volume, air entry and awareness together. A falling rate with worsening fatigue is not necessarily the return to a healthy normal breathing pattern.
应一起看努力、潮气量、进气及意识。频率下降却越来越累，不一定是恢复健康正常呼吸。

00:19:22.824 --> 00:19:32.880
Support ineffective breathing promptly through the trained pathway. Supplemental oxygen may improve saturation without solving the ventilation failure.
应依受训流程及时支持无效呼吸。补氧可能改善饱和度，却未解决通气失败。

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:43.104
First decide whether the measured pH is below, above or within the chosen reference. Acidemia and alkalemia describe that observed state.
先决定所测pH低于、高于还是位于所选参考。酸血症和碱血症描述这一观察状态。

00:19:43.104 --> 00:19:56.856
Acidosis and alkalosis describe processes that tend to lower or raise pH. Several processes may occur together, so a patient can have an acidosis even when the final pH is not below the range.
酸中毒和碱中毒描述倾向降低或升高pH的过程。多个过程可同时存在，因此最终pH未低于范围，也可能仍有酸中毒过程。

00:19:56.856 --> 00:20:07.560
A low pH does not by itself identify a metabolic cause. Look at carbon dioxide, bicarbonate, the clinical history and the possibility of a mixed disorder.
pH低本身不能确定代谢性原因，还需看CO2、碳酸氢根、临床史及混合紊乱可能。

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:19.680
Avoid the candidate fixed fatal-pH statements as universal boundaries. A severe derangement warrants urgent patient-linked assessment, not a deterministic prediction from one number.
不能把候选教材固定致死pH当普遍界线。严重紊乱要求紧急联系患者评估，不是凭一个数作必然结局预测。

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:29.016
Respiratory Opposite means that primary carbon dioxide retention tends to lower pH, while primary carbon dioxide loss tends to raise it.
Respiratory Opposite表示原发CO2潴留倾向降低pH，原发CO2丢失倾向升高pH。

00:20:29.016 --> 00:20:40.392
Metabolic Equal compares pH with primary bicarbonate change: lower bicarbonate tends to accompany lower pH, and higher bicarbonate tends to accompany higher pH.
Metabolic Equal比较pH与原发碳酸氢根变化：碳酸氢根低倾向伴pH低，碳酸氢根高倾向伴pH高。

00:20:40.392 --> 00:20:50.952
ROME does not mean all three numbers must move together or that a compensatory change is a second primary diagnosis. Use the whole pattern and the clinical story.
ROME不表示三个数必须一起变，也不表示代偿变化就是第二原发诊断。要看整组模式及临床经过。

00:20:50.952 --> 00:21:01.872
It also does not judge arterial oxygenation or exclude mixed disorders. Finish by explaining what the patient needs, not by announcing that the mnemonic has been completed.
它也不判断动脉氧合或排除混合紊乱。最后要解释患者需要什么，而不是宣布口诀完成。

00:21:01.872 --> 00:21:14.928
A basic respiratory acidosis pattern is low pH with high carbon dioxide. It can occur with respiratory depression, severe obstruction or another failure of effective alveolar ventilation.
基本呼吸性酸中毒模式是pH低、CO2高，可见于呼吸抑制、严重阻塞或其他有效肺泡通气失败。

00:21:14.928 --> 00:21:26.496
Early bicarbonate may be near baseline; with chronic adaptation it may rise. A high bicarbonate does not automatically turn the result into primary metabolic alkalosis.
早期碳酸氢根可接近基线，慢性适应时可升高。因此高碳酸氢根不自动把结果变成原发代谢性碱中毒。

00:21:26.496 --> 00:21:38.832
Look for shallow breathing, fatigue, reduced air entry and falling awareness. A patient receiving oxygen may keep a reassuring saturation while carbon dioxide rises.
应看浅呼吸、疲惫、进气少及意识下降。正在补氧的患者，CO2上升时仍可能保持看着放心的饱和度。

00:21:38.832 --> 00:21:50.904
Provide the indicated trained ventilation support and cause-appropriate care; do not wait for another sample before treating obvious failure. Reassess response and arrange additional help.
应提供有指征的受训通气支持及适合病因的照护，明显失败时不能等另一份标本再处理，并复评及安排额外支援。

00:21:50.904 --> 00:22:02.424
The simple pattern is high pH and low carbon dioxide from ventilation exceeding carbon dioxide production. Lightheadedness or tingling can occur but does not identify the cause.
简单模式是通气相对CO2产生过多，出现pH高、CO2低。头晕或刺麻可出现，却不能指出病因。

00:22:02.424 --> 00:22:15.360
Consider hypoxemia, infection, pulmonary vascular disease, pain or toxins as well as anxiety. A frightened patient can still have a serious medical cause of rapid breathing.
除焦虑外，还需考虑低氧、感染、肺血管病、疼痛或毒物。害怕的患者仍可有严重医学原因导致快呼吸。

00:22:15.360 --> 00:22:27.504
Do not use paper-bag rebreathing to correct the number. It can reduce inspired oxygen and harm patients whose apparent hyperventilation reflects hypoxemia or myocardial ischemia.
不能用纸袋复吸纠正数值，它会减少吸入氧，伤害实际因低氧或心肌缺血而看似过度通气的患者。

00:22:27.504 --> 00:22:39.480
Reassure while assessing rather than using reassurance as a diagnostic test. The destination and urgency depend on the complete evaluation, not a presumed benign label.
应一边安抚一边评估，而不是把安抚当诊断测试。目的地和紧急度取决于完整评估，不是预设良性标签。

00:22:39.480 --> 00:22:52.944
A basic metabolic acidosis pattern has low pH with low bicarbonate. Added acid, gastrointestinal bicarbonate loss or impaired renal acid excretion can produce this relationship.
基本代谢性酸中毒模式是pH低、碳酸氢根低，可能来自加酸、胃肠丢失碳酸氢根或肾排酸受损。

00:22:52.944 --> 00:23:03.384
Consider the mechanism in the history: dehydration with ketones, shock-related illness, diarrhea or renal failure are not all the same disease or the same fluid plan.
应联系病史机制：脱水伴酮体、休克相关疾病、腹泻或肾衰，不都是同一种病，也不能用同一补液计划。

00:23:03.384 --> 00:23:16.152
The respiratory response may lower carbon dioxide through increased effective ventilation. Deep breathing may be compensatory, not merely emotional distress that should be slowed without assessment.
呼吸反应可通过增加有效通气降低CO2。深呼吸可能是代偿，不只是情绪紧张，不能未评估就让它慢下来。

00:23:16.152 --> 00:23:29.064
Treat immediate threats and the cause through the authorized pathway. A low bicarbonate is not an automatic order for bicarbonate medication, and a normalizing pH is not proof the cause is gone.
应依获授权路径处理即时威胁及病因。碳酸氢根低不自动是给碳酸氢钠指令，pH趋正常也不证明病因消失。

00:23:29.064 --> 00:23:41.472
A basic metabolic alkalosis pattern has high pH with relatively high bicarbonate. Gastric acid loss, certain diuretics and other renal or hormonal processes can contribute.
基本代谢性碱中毒模式是pH高、碳酸氢根相对高，胃酸丢失、某些利尿药及其他肾脏或激素过程可参与。

00:23:41.472 --> 00:23:52.728
Ask about vomiting, medications, intake and the underlying illness. Do not assume vomiting and diarrhea create the same acid-base pattern because both lose fluid.
应问呕吐、药物、摄入及基础疾病。不能因呕吐和腹泻都丢液，就假设酸碱模式相同。

00:23:52.728 --> 00:24:04.656
Respiratory compensation may retain carbon dioxide, but adequate oxygenation limits that response. Deliberately creating inadequate breathing is not a routine corrective maneuver.
呼吸代偿可能保留CO2，但维持足够氧合会限制反应。故意造成呼吸不足，不是常规纠正动作。

00:24:04.656 --> 00:24:15.936
Use the patient state, electrolytes when available and the actual care pathway. A single direction label does not supply a safe replacement-fluid or medication prescription.
应依患者状态、可取得的电解质及真实照护路径。一个方向标签，不能提供安全的补液或药物处方。

00:24:15.936 --> 00:24:29.760
The body can move pH toward baseline through another system. In primary respiratory disease, renal bicarbonate handling adapts over time; in primary metabolic disease, ventilation can respond sooner.
机体可通过另一系统使pH靠近基线。原发呼吸病时，肾脏碳酸氢根处理随时间适应；原发代谢病时，通气可较快响应。

00:24:29.760 --> 00:24:40.032
Time and function matter. Chronic carbon dioxide retention and a sudden new ventilatory failure do not have the same expected bicarbonate pattern.
时间和功能很重要。慢性CO2潴留与突发新通气失败，不会有同一预期碳酸氢根模式。

00:24:40.032 --> 00:24:52.512
A compensatory direction does not prove the response is appropriate in size, and a normal pH does not prove a benign fully compensated state. More than one primary problem may coexist.
方向像代偿，不证明幅度合适；pH正常也不证明是良性完全代偿状态。多个原发问题可能同时存在。

00:24:52.512 --> 00:25:05.352
This introductory lesson does not replace a full mixed-disorder assessment. Explain the likely pattern and uncertainty, then use the appropriate clinical review instead of overstating certainty.
本入门课不能替代完整混合紊乱分析。应解释可能模式及不确定，再寻适当临床复核，不能夸大确定性。

00:25:05.352 --> 00:25:19.416
In an original assumed arterial result, pH is seven point four zero, carbon dioxide twenty and bicarbonate twelve. The pH is within range, but two major variables are clearly abnormal.
原创假设动脉结果为pH 7.40、CO2 20、碳酸氢根12。pH在范围内，但另两个主要变量明显异常。

00:25:19.416 --> 00:25:30.864
Do not stop at normal or automatically call the patient fully compensated. Opposing respiratory and metabolic processes can produce a deceptively ordinary final pH.
不能停在正常，也不能自动称完全代偿。相反的呼吸和代谢过程可形成看似普通的最终pH。

00:25:30.864 --> 00:25:44.040
A trained expected-compensation review can reveal that the carbon dioxide is lower than expected for a simple metabolic acidosis. The likely interpretation needs the clinical story, not the mnemonic alone.
受训的预期代偿分析可显示，CO2低于简单代谢性酸中毒预期。可能解释需临床经过，不能只靠口诀。

00:25:44.040 --> 00:25:54.024
The case teaches why you preserve the full report and seek appropriate help. It does not turn a classroom example into a medication or destination rule.
此例说明为何需保留完整报告并寻适当帮助，不把课堂例题变成用药或目的地规则。

00:25:54.024 --> 00:26:06.888
Take another original assumed arterial result: pH seven point two eight, carbon dioxide thirty-one and bicarbonate fourteen. First identify acidemia and the low bicarbonate.
再看原创假设动脉结果：pH 7.28、CO2 31、碳酸氢根14。先识别酸血症及碳酸氢根低。

00:26:06.888 --> 00:26:17.280
The pattern supports a metabolic acidosis with a respiratory response, rather than calling the low carbon dioxide a separate respiratory alkalosis automatically.
这一模式支持代谢性酸中毒伴呼吸反应，不能自动把低CO2另叫呼吸性碱中毒。

00:26:17.280 --> 00:26:28.992
The linked reading shows a limited expected-response calculation for this example. In practice, the cause and the patient state still determine the urgency and the authorized treatment.
下方阅读展示此例有限的预期反应计算。实际工作中，病因及患者状态仍决定紧急度及获授权治疗。

00:26:28.992 --> 00:26:41.448
Look for the history that fits, such as losses, renal illness or metabolic disease, while supporting perfusion and watching breathing. Do not invent a diagnosis from these three numbers alone.
应找相符病史，例如丢失、肾病或代谢病，同时支持灌注并观察呼吸，不能仅凭三个数编定诊断。

00:26:41.448 --> 00:26:55.344
In an original community-theatre encounter, a sixty-four-year-old with obstructive lung disease becomes exhausted. Supplemental oxygen improves saturation, but breaths become smaller and awareness falls.
原创社区剧场现场中，一位64岁阻塞性肺病患者逐渐疲竭。补氧后饱和度改善，但呼吸变小、意识下降。

00:26:55.344 --> 00:27:10.368
For the classroom, assume an arterial result of pH seven point two five, carbon dioxide sixty and bicarbonate about twenty-six. This supports a predominantly respiratory acidosis with inadequate ventilation.
课堂假设动脉结果为pH 7.25、CO2 60、碳酸氢根约26，支持以通气不足为主的呼吸性酸中毒。

00:27:10.368 --> 00:27:23.352
The falling respiratory rate is not reassuring in this trajectory. Reassess airway, breathing and circulation, provide effective trained ventilation support and seek appropriate advanced assistance.
在此趋势中，呼吸频率下降并不放心。应重评气道、呼吸和循环，实施有效受训通气支持并寻适当高级支援。

00:27:23.352 --> 00:27:33.936
Do not delay that response to obtain a gas in an unstable patient; the example explains a process that clinical deterioration already requires you to recognize.
不稳定患者不能为取血气而延误反应。此例只是解释临床恶化已经要求识别的过程。

00:27:33.936 --> 00:27:45.768
The Week Six Wednesday work includes a rapid ETCO2 fall after return of circulation. Treat that as a prompt for immediate reassessment, not one certain diagnosis.
第6周周三任务包括恢复循环后ETCO2快速下降。应将其当即时重评提示，不是某个确定诊断。

00:27:45.768 --> 00:28:00.312
Assess the patient for recurrent arrest or reduced cardiac output while checking airway, ventilation and the sampling circuit. A disconnection, altered ventilation or poor perfusion can produce different responses.
应评患者是否再次骤停或心排下降，同时检查气道、通气及取样回路。脱接、通气改变或灌注差，需要不同反应。

00:28:00.312 --> 00:28:13.056
Do not increase ventilation reflexively because the carbon dioxide is already low. Overventilation can worsen a circulation problem; respond to the actual cause and clinical state.
CO2已低时，不能反射性加通气。过度通气可使循环问题更差，应依真实原因和临床状态处理。

00:28:13.056 --> 00:28:25.608
Keep school post-ROSC targets distinct from current local guideline differences already taught in Week Five. A target band never replaces immediate recognition of an ineffective breath or pulse.
应把学校复苏后目标与第5周已讲的现行当地差异分开。目标区间永远不能替代即时识别无效呼吸或无效循环。

00:28:25.608 --> 00:28:39.312
The school uses pH below seven point two zero as a red-flag example. Marked derangement deserves urgent attention, but the number alone is not a universal ICU-destination or impending-arrest rule.
学校以pH低于7.20举红旗示例。严重紊乱需要紧急关注，但数值单独不是普遍ICU目的地或即将骤停规则。

00:28:39.312 --> 00:28:51.744
Determine the patient needs now and the capability needed next. Geography, instability, available support and actual regional agreements affect the safest receiving pathway.
应确定患者现在及下一步需要什么能力。地理、不稳定程度、可用支援及真实区域约定，会影响最安全接收路径。

00:28:51.744 --> 00:29:03.912
Mild respiratory alkalosis does not prove anxiety or a safe routine destination, and apparently compensated COPD does not establish safety during a new deterioration.
轻度呼吸性碱中毒不证明焦虑或常规目的地安全；看似已代偿的COPD，在新恶化时也不证明安全。

00:29:03.912 --> 00:29:14.232
Do not delay needed support or conveyance while waiting for an unavailable test. Give an early, patient-linked pre-alert and coordinate the appropriate resource.
不能等无法取得的检测而延误所需支持或转运。应尽早结合患者预警，并协调适当资源。

00:29:14.232 --> 00:29:26.328
Give the receiving team a coherent sequence, not an ECG label followed by disconnected laboratory numbers. Start with the patient and why the situation is time-sensitive.
应给接收团队连贯顺序，不是先甩ECG名称再堆不相连化验数。要先患者及为何有时效性。

00:29:26.328 --> 00:29:39.216
Describe the interpretable tracing and what changed, then give the actual gas type, values, units, time and oxygen or ventilation state. State any sample-quality concern explicitly.
先描述可解释记录及变化，再给真实血气类型、数值、单位、时间及给氧或通气状态，明确标本质量疑问。

00:29:39.216 --> 00:29:52.128
Distinguish observation from interpretation, including the likely acid-base process and unresolved alternatives. Avoid reporting venous oxygen as arterial or a normal pH as no disorder.
要区分观察与解释，包括可能酸碱过程及未解决替代原因。不能把静脉氧报成动脉，也不能把正常pH报成无紊乱。

00:29:52.128 --> 00:30:04.872
Finish with actual treatment, response and the next request, and confirm the message was received. A precise handover supports continued care while definitive diagnosis is still developing.
最后给实际治疗、反应和下一请求，并确认收到。即使确定诊断仍在发展，准确交接也能支持持续照护。

00:30:04.872 --> 00:30:17.784
You should be able to read a useful ECG systematically, recognize important ischemic or rhythm concerns and explain why neither a guaranteed cascade nor a single normal tracing is safe reasoning.
现在应能系统阅读有用ECG，识别重要缺血或心律怀疑，并解释为何必然演变顺序或单次正常记录都不是安全推理。

00:30:17.784 --> 00:30:28.536
For a gas, identify sample type and context before using reference values. Separate oxygen tension from saturation, content and delivery.
血气先确认标本类型及背景，再用参考值，并区分氧分压、饱和度、含量与输送。

00:30:28.536 --> 00:30:42.864
Explain the four primary patterns and why compensation or normal pH needs further context. Use the original worked examples and bilingual reading to reconstruct the mechanism rather than memorizing arrows alone.
应解释四种原发模式，并说明为何代偿或正常pH仍需背景。用原创例题及中英阅读重建机制，不只背箭头。

00:30:42.864 --> 00:30:56.448
Finally name the actual threat and next action, including when to stop testing and support the patient. The remainder of the weekend applies this reasoning to advanced respiratory, twelve-lead and multisystem practice.
最后说出实际威胁及下一行动，包括何时停检测支持患者。本周余下教学会把这些推理用于高级呼吸、十二导联和多系统演练。
